00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.530
So, for those who don't
know about the show,

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.790
tell them kind of what it's about.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.430
- I'm the worst pitch
person, but we're gonna try.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.360
- I can't wait.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.009
- Okay.
(Juliette and Kelly laughs)

00:03:08.009 --> 00:03:09.118
- Yeah.

00:03:09.118 --> 00:03:09.960
- No, no.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:10.793
Okay, wait.

00:03:10.793 --> 00:03:12.720
A group of teens in the '90s,

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.020
they're on a little soccer team.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.560
Their plane crashes, and
it's all these things they do

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.840
to survive in the wilderness.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:22.770
We-
- That we don't know.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.630
- That we don't know what they do.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:25.680
- Yeah.
- Yet.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.790
- You're finding out slowly.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.230
- We're gonna find out slowly,

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:31.020
and then there's the
older versions of them

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.630
which is myself, Melanie Lynskey-

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.500
- Christina Ricci.
- Christina Ricci.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.760
Tawny Cypress.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.800
And two new additions,
(audience cheering)

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.680
Lauren Ambrose and Simone Kessell.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.000
- Yeah.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.360
- And we are the older
version with all the trauma

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.290
and the secrets we keep, and
a lot of us act very strange.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:50.310
- Yeah, you do.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.510
- They do strange things.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.990
I feel like my character's the
most sane 'cause her pain is

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.524
just kind of obvious.
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:56.524 --> 00:03:57.357
(audience laughs)

00:03:57.357 --> 00:03:58.620
The other girls like kill things.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:03:59.453
- I love that you think

00:03:59.453 --> 00:04:00.675
yours is sane.
(audience laughs)

00:04:00.675 --> 00:04:01.530
(laughs) I love...

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:02.648
- She's volatile-
- So, she...

00:04:02.648 --> 00:04:03.779
(Kelly laughs)
- Sad.

00:04:03.779 --> 00:04:04.612
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:04:04.612 --> 00:04:06.300
All the fun things to put into one thing.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.320
So your dad,

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.930
you said your dad raised you
to be a quitter (laughs).

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.864
- Oh, this is my favorite line.

00:04:11.864 --> 00:04:13.470
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:15.480
- Why?
(audience exclaims)

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.313
- Oh my God. Adorable.
- Oh my God.

00:04:16.313 --> 00:04:17.520
Am I gonna cry again?

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:18.353
I'm not even-
- Here.

00:04:18.353 --> 00:04:20.073
Look, I'm here for you.
- I'm not even premenstrual.

00:04:20.073 --> 00:04:20.906
(audience laughs)
- I'm not even... (laughs)

00:04:20.906 --> 00:04:21.739
- What the (beep) is happening?

00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:22.582
(Kelly clapping)
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:22.582 --> 00:04:24.372
Oh my God, and you blew it up.

00:04:24.372 --> 00:04:25.529
(audience cheering)
Oh my god (laughs).

00:04:25.529 --> 00:04:27.545
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:27.545 --> 00:04:28.628
- I love you.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:30.533
Wait, so what...

00:04:30.533 --> 00:04:32.130
Oh my God. You're fine.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.330
I'm about to hug you-

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.163
- Why-
- But that might make

00:04:34.163 --> 00:04:35.108
it worse.
- No, no.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.750
And I'm crying over joyful things.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.520
- Yeah, no it's beautiful.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.290
I love this picture too.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.095
But why do you think he
raised you to be a quitter?

00:04:43.095 --> 00:04:44.850
(Kelly and Juliette laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:45.930
Just curious.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.096
- Because he was a pushover.

00:04:48.096 --> 00:04:50.880
I went to gymnastics and
then the girls were mean.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.130
They're like, "Hey, a flea
is jumping out of your hair."

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.410
I was eight.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.243
I was like, "Ooh,"

00:04:55.243 --> 00:04:56.130
and I'm like, "What?"

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.570
You know, they're just making (beep) up

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:59.100
to be evil and mean.
- Yeah (laughs).

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.300
- So he would just what, let you-

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.280
- So, the different things,

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.700
if I got pissed off or shut down,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.730
he'd be like, "So, don't go.
You don't have to go back."

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:09.750
So that was that.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.670
But however, like karate,

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.680
I would like to be a black belt right now.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.972
I never made it past brown

00:05:15.972 --> 00:05:16.805
(Kelly laughs)
'cause I don't know,

00:05:16.805 --> 00:05:18.512
maybe I was tired one day.

00:05:18.512 --> 00:05:19.345
(audience laughs)
But I

00:05:19.345 --> 00:05:21.010
coulda used the discipline.
- He didn't pushed you?

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.250
Yeah.
- I like karate discipline

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.320
and then singing-
- I need you

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.390
to tell my children this.
- Teachers.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:28.650
Yeah.
- Because I make my children

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:29.483
finish things out.

00:05:29.483 --> 00:05:31.110
- Really?
- And I get crap for it.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.480
And I'm like, "You don't
have to do it next time

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:36.060
but you're definitely gonna
finish what mama paid for.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:36.900
'Cause mama grew up
- Yes.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.280
- In a duplex in an apartment

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.780
and I did not have a lot of money."

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.040
And even though you have money,

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.540
you still don't like to waste it.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.830
And it's like you gotta teach them,

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:44.940
they have to follow through.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.790
- Well, that's my sister
and it's the smarter move.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:48.779
If I had kids...

00:05:48.779 --> 00:05:52.020
I'm the Lucille Ball of aunts,

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:52.853
I like to say,
(audience laughs)

00:05:52.853 --> 00:05:53.686
like the auntie.

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.890
I know people associate me with cool,

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.426
but I'm really like (laughs),

00:05:57.426 --> 00:05:58.290
(Kelly laughs)
"Hey, guys."

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.550
And I'm really like
(audience laughs)

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:00.930
prudent with them.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.460
- Yeah.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.370
- But what I wanted to say, I
think that's the correct way.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:09.390
Encourage someone to
finish through the hardship

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.240
of some things.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.320
But I did have a ballet
teacher that when I had...

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.440
It's weird 'cause it did
good and bad things for me.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.143
I had a ballet teacher,
I had ripped tights,

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.270
we didn't have much money.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.227
I was living with my mom and I was like,

00:06:26.227 --> 00:06:27.660
"Oh, maybe she won't notice."

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:31.230
And I just had leg warmers, I
was like seven, and a leotard.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.150
And I show up, it's the first thing.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:36.960
She goes, "Now, see? This is
what I've been telling you

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.508
about presentation."

00:06:38.508 --> 00:06:39.990
(Kelly exclaims)
"Look at Juliette."

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:43.200
And I'm like, I'm seven,
and noticing I've-

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.257
- Oh, that's not cool.

00:06:44.257 --> 00:06:48.240
- It wasn't cool, and I never went back.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.260
That's my big move.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.252
I was like, "I'm done with you."

00:06:51.252 --> 00:06:52.740
(audience laughs)
And that served me well

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.790
in certain things.

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.470
- Yeah, I agree with that

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.360
because we had a similar moment happen.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.330
I had the shoes that you got
from a store that cost like...

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.640
You know, they were like
6.99 for tennis shoes,

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.500
and that's where we shopped.
- Casual (speaks faintly).

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.333
- Yeah.

00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:06.180
And a great store, by the way,

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.500
for people that don't have a lot of money.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:09.870
And so anyways, so I played basketball

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.970
and I made marks on the floor, I guess.

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:13.920
And I didn't know my
shoes were making marks

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.477
but the coach put us all
aside and he was like,

00:07:16.477 --> 00:07:17.940
"Look at your shoes.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.800
Whose shoes are making all
these marks on the floor?"

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.900
And I didn't even realize,

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.017
and then I kept hearing all the girls go,

00:07:23.017 --> 00:07:25.833
"Those are cheap shoes, only
cheap shoes make those marks."

00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:28.020
(audience exclaims)
And I had never...

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.596
I walked out of the gym and I was like...

00:07:30.596 --> 00:07:32.513
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:07:32.513 --> 00:07:35.339
I was like, "Don't make a move."

00:07:35.339 --> 00:07:38.020
I was like, "Whose shoes did that?"

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:38.909
(Juliette laughs)
- I was like

00:07:38.909 --> 00:07:40.860
(audience laughs)
so tacky.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.930
I was mortified, and it did,

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:43.890
and then I had to go back-

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:45.520
- [Juliette] Oh, God.
- In the same shoes.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:46.950
- What?
- Because my mom couldn't

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.180
afford anything else.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.013
We didn't have money.

00:07:49.013 --> 00:07:50.220
And I had to go back in the same shoes

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:52.350
because my mom was like,
"You're finishing it out."

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:53.970
And I'm glad she made me finish it out.

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:55.950
But those moments, teachers should know,

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.314
people should know better.

00:07:57.314 --> 00:07:58.147
- Yeah, they-
- To point that out

00:07:58.147 --> 00:08:00.210
'cause some people can't
afford the other option.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.500
- That is the biggest thing.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.250
I remember flip-flopping my pants

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:09.060
I'll wear these and then
the same ones on Wednesday,

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:11.520
maybe they won't notice,
like all that stuff.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.830
But that's so sad that
teacher had no idea,

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:16.050
the one little fear like,
"Ah, I have cheap shoes."

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:16.883
No one will know.

